 gross incivility;
 harassment;
 spamming;
 deliberately tripping the edit filter;
 breaching the policies or guidelines, especially sockpuppetry;
 attempts to coerce actions of editors through threats of actions outside the Wikipedia processes, whether onsite or offsite;
 advising, commanding, comforting, counseling, or suggesting another editor to disruptively edit.

Edit warring, especially breaches of the three-revert rule, often results in a block, either from the pages the user is disrupting or from the entire site.

